From: Arvind Venkataramani
 <250267+arvindvenkataramani@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 19 Sep 2026 02:05:49 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] fix(tts/pocket): tokenize around unknown characters and
 size chunks on normalized text
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

- SentencePieceTokenizer: one scalar with no vocabulary piece no longer sends the whole input to per-character fallback; the lattice gets an edge past it, scored below every real piece, and the scalar is emitted as its UTF-8 byte-fallback pieces
- chunkTextWithMetadata: collapse whitespace before splitting and counting, through a collapseWhitespace helper shared with normalizeText, so a chunk is sized on the text it is synthesized from
- Fixes garbled speech for text containing ( ) [ ] / # @ … and similar, and the mid-phrase cut in the first sentence after a paragraph break
- Token ids now equal the reference sentencepiece library's on the English tokenizer.model
- Tests build a synthetic vocabulary, so they need no model download
